License decision (v2.1 section 8)
--------------------------------
sticker-convert upstream: https://github.com/laggykiller/sticker-convert
Evidence checked: GitHub API `/license` reports `gpl-2.0`; `pyproject.toml` uses
`license={file="LICENSE"}` with a GPLv2 classifier; `LICENSE` is the GPLv2 text;
`sticker-convert.appdata.xml` declares `<project_license>GPL-2.0+</project_license>`,
which is the author-maintained AppStream project-license identifier equivalent to
GPL-2.0-or-later. Following the v2.1 decision tree, this project therefore adopts
GPL-3.0-only. Apache-2.0 dependencies are compatible with GPL-3.0; no GPL-extra
restrictions are imposed. All prior MIT / no-paid-distribution wording is removed.

Reused upstream logic / files
-----------------------------
1) sticker-convert (GPL-2.0-or-later), commit inspected 2026-11-15.
   Reused as conceptual reference and test fixture source:
   - `tests/samples/animated_tgs_512x512_1s.tgs` conceptual TGS metadata fixture
     (gzip Lottie JSON: v5.2.1, 60 fps, 512-class canvas); no upstream Python code
     was copied into the Android app.
